{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevK2Z14vjgT56iYqwhiV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) which are handled by GlobalExceptionHandler at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28`\n- Error responses use consistent envelope with code, message, and fields (ErrorCode enum at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`)\n- Repositories use in-memory ConcurrentHashMap\n- Tests use MockMvc and assert response body structure, not just status\n- HTTP 201 for resource creation, 404 for not found, 409 for conflict\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - must add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order and create OrderStatus enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` - must add cancel endpoint and inject ShipmentRepository\n3. `ShipmentController.kt` - must add validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n4. `ApiError.kt` - must add new error code(s) for shipment-on-cancelled-order scenario\n5. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - must add tests for cancel endpoint and new order status field\n6. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - must add test for shipment creation rejection on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Backward compatibility: Order now requires a status field in responses; existing clients may not handle it\n- Concurrency: ConcurrentHashMap doesn't guarantee atomic multi-step operations (checking CONFIRMED shipments before cancelling); the ticket says \"all-or-nothing\"\n- The idempotent retry case (cancelling already-cancelled order) must work exactly as specified\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket is explicit about all cases.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class, and create an OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException with 404\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with the order (idempotent)\n   - If ACTIVE, check all shipments: if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with 409 and change nothing\n   - If all shipments are CREATED or absent, mark order as CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, persist, return 200 with the order\n   - Inject InMemoryShipmentRepository to check shipment statuses\n\n3. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the create method, check if the target order exists and is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException with 409.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt**: Add error code `ORDER_CANCELLED` to signal \"cannot create shipment for cancelled order\".\n\n5. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds and changes status\n   - Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipment rejects with 409\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - GET /orders/{orderId} reports the status\n\n6. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:** \nI considered adding a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic, but the existing codebase has no service layer—all logic lives in repositories and controllers. Adding one would be unrelated refactoring and exceed the scope of the ticket. The controller can safely orchestrate the cancel logic directly.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n**Case 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with only CREATED shipments**\n- Read: Order from repository, all shipments for that orderId\n- Check: Order exists (404 if not), order is ACTIVE, no CONFIRMED shipments\n- Write: Order status → CANCELLED, all CREATED shipments status → CANCELLED\n- Return: 200 OK with updated Order\n\n**Case 2: Cancel already-CANCELLED order**\n- Read: Order from repository\n- Check: Order exists (404 if not)\n- Write: None (idempotent)\n- Return: 200 OK with Order\n\n**Case 3: Cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment**\n- Read: Order from repository, all shipments for that orderId\n- Check: Order exists (404 if not), at least one shipment is CONFIRMED\n- Write: None (all-or-nothing: revert any partial changes)\n- Return: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n**Case 4: Create shipment for non-existent order**\n- Current behavior: succeeds (no validation that orderId exists)\n- No change required by this ticket\n\n**Case 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order**\n- Read: Order from repository\n- Check: Order is not CANCELLED (409 if it is)\n- Write: Shipment in CREATED status\n- Return: 409 Conflict if order is CANCELLED, else 201 Created\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest changes**: \n   - `creates an order with status ACTIVE` - new test to verify status field exists and is ACTIVE on creation\n   - `cancels an active order and returns status CANCELLED` - cancel ACTIVE order, verify response has status CANCELLED\n   - `cancels an already cancelled order and returns status CANCELLED (idempotent)` - cancel twice, second succeeds without error\n   - `rejects cancel when order has a confirmed shipment` - create order, create shipment, manually set to CONFIRMED, cancel should reject\n   - `returns 404 when cancelling unknown order` - cancel non-existent orderId\n   - `cancels all created shipments when cancelling active order` - create order, create multiple CREATED shipments, cancel order, verify shipments are CANCELLED\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest changes**:\n   - `rejects shipment creation for cancelled order` - create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, expect 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**The first line of code comes after this marker.**\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start by modifying the Order class to add the status field."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3298,"cache_read_input_tokens":18892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3298},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86251467-3571-41d0-9dc9-ad97cc8fbc58","uuid":"9bf54887-0422-4bbf-b862-71a936ca54ee","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:29:15.660Z","request_id":"req_011CevK2Y2mtkR6K5bp9CiHk"}
